kind how-do-i
title How do I show a terminal on a display that reports no EDID?
intro Without a udev daemon, vtium can match a display only by its monitor's EDID, its identity. A display that reports none can still show a terminal through a rule for every display. vtium-config says which of the two a path can use before it calls the path complete.
see heads-and-rules/show-a-terminal-on-a-display
waits-for a new finding of this card: NEW PATH calls a path with such a display complete, and a then refuses it as a rule the person never wrote

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
device display HDMI-A-1
device keyboard 046d:c31c USB Keyboard

1. Go to the Flow tab.
2. Highlight HDMI-A-1.
3. Press Space to pick.
4. Highlight USB Keyboard.
5. Press Space to pick.
6. Press a to add path.
at the path
check screen lacks "This is not a valid rule"
check screen lacks "Write it as `display MATCH -> TARGET`"
